Subject: [PATCH] fonts: Windows script fallback table under a Windows profile

Under a Windows profile, Linux font fallback picks families from
Windows' own per-script candidate lists, copied unchanged from the
upstream Windows fallback code. The table covers kana, Traditional Han,
Hangul, Cyrillic, Greek, Thai, Latin and the other scripts Windows
lists. A candidate is used only when the host has it and it covers the
character, and Fontconfig decides otherwise. Text measured over an
uncovered character then follows a Windows machine's fallback choice
wherever the host has that font.

